# sandbox-configs: the job and cluster descriptions that cloudflow reads.
# Read by exportit/tools/export.py; described in exportit/MAP.md.
#
# Both directories, every file, unchanged and with their identifiers in them
# (stage 6, decision 1), templates and site data together (decision 2). They
# keep their names, so that the paths in cloudflow's documentation still hold.

covers job.configs/
covers cluster.configs/
copy job.configs/        job.configs/
copy cluster.configs/    cluster.configs/

# Files that exist only in the unit.
new README.md
new LICENSE                # a copy of the repository's LICENSE
new Justfile
new pyproject.toml
new uv.lock
new .python-version
new schema/                # written by exportit/tools/configs_schema.py from cloudflow's code
new tests/
new attic/                 # descriptions that could not be repaired, each with its reason (spec 005)
new .gitignore   # the unit's own, since it is a repository of its own (MOVINGDAY.md)
new .specify/     # Spec Kit 1.2.3 and the constitution (MOVINGDAY.md, M4)
new .claude/      # Spec Kit's skills
new CLAUDE.md     # written by `just constitution`

# Its originals were deleted from Cloud-Sandbox by stage 22, step 4 (2026-11-19):
# the unit owns its copied files, and only its lineage is checked.
owned
